    "Kaplan-Meier estimates show no significant differences in outcomes like death, stroke, and myocardial infarction (MI) between Carotid Endarterectomy (CEA) and Carotid Artery Stenting (CAS) at 30 and 365 days post-procedure. Meta-analyses indicate no major differences between CEA and CAS regarding major short-term outcomes, though CAS may have higher rates of periprocedural strokes. The SAPPHIRE study demonstrated technical success in asymptomatic patients with a 30-day stroke, MI, or death incidence difference between CAS (4.8%) and CEA (9.8%). The CAVATAS trial highlighted similar stroke or death rates at 30 days between CAS and CEA but noted specific procedural complications.": null
